I think the Tourist class is great, but would be even better with a few
improvements. E.g.:

1. The camera should have a roll of film which can be developed at a special
shop (or maybe just a general store).

Intelligent (?) monsters should pose for photographs (or maybe it would be
funnier for unintelligent monsters? e.g.
 "The acid blob smiles cheesely and strikes a pose.")
Maybe they could ask you to do it again to get one of their good side? Or
request a couple of 6 x 13's for their grandchildren.

"Here's a couple of snaps we took in the dungeon of doom last vacation..."

or come across a group of monsters huddled around a photo album: Vampires
"...and here's a knight I sucked dry last summer..."
or
"Boy, they don't make them like they used to, do they?"

Maybe photograph albums might even have some useful properties: e.g. Identify
a few items (recognise them).

"You show the photograph to the Gelatinous cube." -more-
"It pines for its lost sweetheart..."

"You resist the Succubus's advances, but give her a few poleroids instead."

"The Succubus falls in love with the photograph."

Or a new attack:
apply - photo album
"You show the holiday snaps to the troll..."
"After a few hours, the Troll falls asleep."

The possibilities for this are almost endless!


2. The same sort of thing could be done with an autograph book. Selling famous
autographs to shops.


3. The Tourists should also be able to ask for directions by #chatting to
monsters. E.g: Information about the nearest stores.


So this might be a bit complicated, but I think the Tourist would be a much
better class if the humour element was brought out more. Nobody really plays
a tourist with the same seriousness as a Barbarian, do they?

